# AGENT REFERENCE: ASSETS

## Quick Context

- Responsibility: preserve asset metadata/blob relationships, menu payloads, and operator upload behavior.
- Confirmed contracts: asset UUIDs, content relationships, supported types, and client-visible payload fields require migration evidence.
- Top defects: destructive basename overwrite, DB/blob non-atomicity, broken write APIs, import-time filesystem work, and uncertain production media serving.
- Target disposition: retain asset capability behind explicit storage/service boundaries; generic writable REST is transitional.
- Read next: load behavior review only when terminal/menu payloads also change.

## 0. Rules

1. Treat `server/assets`, current storage paths, API serializers, and direct consumers as authoritative; use generated schema and deployment configuration as supporting evidence.
2. Preserve confirmed identifiers, media formats, and menu payloads, not public mutation, broken upload behavior, unsafe overwrite semantics, or orphaned files.
3. Keep HTTP transport, file validation, metadata persistence, blob storage, URL generation, and downstream menu delivery separate.
4. Make authorization, content validation, size limits, overwrite/delete policy, transaction boundaries, and cache identity explicit.

## 1. Sources

- Primary: `server/assets/models/{files,games,input}.py`, `server/assets/serializers.py`, `server/assets/views.py`, `server/assets/urls.py`, `server/assets/storages.py`, `server/assets/validators/{asset_validators,file_validator}.py`, and `server/assets/admin.py`
- Persistence: `server/assets/migrations/0001_initial.py` and `server/core/models/base.py`
- Entrypoints: `/api/assets/` DRF router, custom Django admin at `/admin/`, and media requests under `/media`
- Direct consumers: `server/peripheral_behavior/models/menu.py`, `server/peripheral_behavior/serializers/menu.py`, `server/peripheral_behavior/admin.py`, and `server/peripheral_devices/serializers/api.py`
- Runtime/deployment dependencies: `server/core/urls.py`, `server/core/views.py`, `server/core/helpers.py`, `server/settings.py`, `docker-compose.yml`, and `docker/nginx/conf.d/default.conf`
- Evidence: `schema.yml`. No source tests, fixtures, or asset-specific documentation cover this package.

## 2. Structure

| Path/component | Responsibility | Consumers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `models.files.SkabenFile` | Shared UUID/name/hash behavior and filesystem URI | binary/text asset models, menu hashing/serialization |
| `AudioFile`, `VideoFile`, `ImageFile` | Persist uploaded binary metadata and storage name | admin, asset API, menu items |
| `TextFile` | Persist editable text and generate a `.txt` blob on every save | admin, asset API, text menu items |
| `models.games.HackGame` | Persist Fallout-style game parameters | asset API; no source-code domain consumer found |
| `models.input.UserInput` | Persist action, expected response, and UI delay | asset API, user-input menu items |
| `storages.OverwriteStorage` | Hard-coded local filesystem storage with delete-before-save replacement | all file models and migrations |
| `validators.FileValidator` | Validate filename-derived extension/MIME and byte length | binary model fields during form/serializer validation |
| `serializers.FileSerializer` | Return absolute filesystem-path-derived URL and writable name | audio/video/image API and nested menu output |
| `views.*ViewSet` | Expose full CRUD for six concrete models | HTTP clients and operator UI |
| `peripheral_behavior.MenuItem*` | Reference assets and incorporate asset hash into menu/account hashes | terminal API/configuration consumers |

| Process/flow | Entrypoint/input | Runtime/output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Binary admin upload | authenticated custom admin form | validate upload, save blob, insert/update metadata |
| Binary API CRUD | `/api/assets/{audiofile|videofile|imagefile}/` | list/retrieve metadata URL; create/update upload contract is broken |
| Text admin edit | authenticated custom admin form | render content into UTF-8 text blob, then persist metadata |
| Text API CRUD | `/api/assets/textfile/` | only `name` and `file` exposed; hidden ident/content get empty values on create |
| Game/input CRUD | `/api/assets/{hackgame|userinput}/` | synchronous ORM CRUD |
| Menu serialization | behavior/device API request | nested asset name/URL or user-input display fields |
| Media delivery | `/media/...` | Nginx proxies request to Django API; Django only adds media-serving routes in debug mode |

## 3. Canonical Flows

### Binary file creation through admin

```text
multipart admin form
  -> model field validation
       -> extension from filename
       -> MIME guessed from filename
       -> byte-size limit
       -> ImageField/Pillow validation for images
  -> FileField upload_to="<kind>/"
  -> OverwriteStorage(location="/media/<kind>/")
  -> physical file /media/<kind>/<kind>/<original-name>
  -> SkabenFile.save(): time/UUID-derived MD5 hash
  -> database row
```

Limits are 30 MiB audio, 120 MiB video, and 5 MiB image. Audio accepts `mp3`, `wav`, `ogg`, `spx`, `oga`, and `webm`; video accepts `webm`, `mp4`, `mp4v`, and `mpg4`; image accepts `png`, `jpg`, `jpeg`, and `webp`.

`OverwriteStorage` removes any existing physical path before writing. Because binary filenames are not namespaced by asset UUID, uploading the same basename for a second record replaces bytes used by the first record. Database records can therefore share one path while carrying different hashes/names.

### Binary API create

```text
POST /api/assets/<kind>/ with name and optional attempted file
  -> FileSerializer treats file as read-only SerializerMethodField
  -> uploaded file ignored/rejected as writable input
  -> model may persist empty file name
  -> response serialization calls obj.file.path
  -> ValueError when no file is associated
```

Observed result is a likely HTTP 500 after an invalid metadata row has already been inserted. OpenAPI exposes `file` as read-only while still advertising full create/update routes. Existing valid rows can be listed/retrieved; file replacement through this serializer is impossible.

### Text file save

```text
TextFile(ident, name, content).save()
  -> build ContentFile(content)
  -> file name <uuid>_<ident>.txt
  -> storage path /media/text/text/<uuid>_<ident>.txt
  -> delete same-name blob if present
  -> write blob before database save
  -> SkabenFile.save() replaces hash with time/UUID-derived MD5
  -> database insert/update
```

The first hash assigned in `TextFile.save()` is overwritten by `SkabenFile.save()`. Changing `ident` produces a new filename and leaves the old blob. Database failure after blob write leaves an orphan. Replacement failure after delete can leave the database pointing to missing content.

### Text API create

```text
POST /api/assets/textfile/ with exposed name/file fields
  -> serializer excludes uuid, hash, ident, and content
  -> TextFile gets empty ident/content
  -> save generates empty text file named <uuid>_.txt
  -> first blank ident may persist
  -> later create conflicts with unique ident=""
```

Any uploaded `file` value is replaced by generated content during model save. This API does not expose the actual editable text contract.

### Menu asset delivery

```text
MenuItemAudio|Video|Image|Text -> asset FK
  -> nested menu serializer
  -> binary: {name, file=<request-host absolute URI>}
  -> text: {name, file=<storage URL>}
  -> menu/account hash includes asset.hash
```

Deleting an asset cascades through its `MenuItem*` foreign keys, deleting referencing menu items. Django does not delete the corresponding filesystem blob automatically.

### Media serving

```text
client GET /media/...
  -> Nginx location /media
  -> proxy to API container
  -> Django static(settings.MEDIA_URL, MEDIA_ROOT)
```

`django.conf.urls.static.static()` serves media only with `DEBUG=True`. Production settings set `DEBUG=False`, Nginx has no `/media` volume/alias, and `/media` is only proxied to Django. Current production topology therefore has no confirmed media-serving path.

## 4. Observed Contracts

### Binary asset models

- Role: named audio, video, or image resource with UUID primary key, stored file name, and cache/change hash.
- Input/state: `name` maximum 128 characters; required `file`; UUID is generated and not editable; hash is database-editable false.
- Storage: hard-coded `OverwriteStorage` roots `/media/audio/`, `/media/video/`, and `/media/image/`, plus matching `upload_to` prefix. Resulting physical path repeats the kind segment.
- Behavior: every model save recalculates hash as MD5 of current Unix second plus UUID. Hash is not a digest of file bytes or metadata.
- Output/effects: menu-item and terminal-account hashes incorporate asset hash; model/admin preview URI concatenates `settings.BASE_URL` with local `file.path`.
- Invariants: UUID identifies database row. Filename/path is not unique in database and storage overwrite makes it shared by basename.
- Edge cases: two saves in one second can retain same hash despite changed data; metadata-only saves in later seconds change hash despite unchanged content; missing file makes `file.path` and preview/serialization fail.

### `TextFile`

- Role: editable text document materialized as a generated text blob.
- Input/state: unique alphanumeric `ident` up to 128 characters, visible `name` up to 128, unrestricted text `content`, nullable/blank file field.
- Behavior: every save writes `content` into `<uuid>_<ident>.txt` before metadata persistence. UTF-8 is used by `ContentFile` for string content.
- Output/effects: physical path is under `/media/text/text/`; model `uri` uses `BASE_URL + file.path`.
- Invariants: `ident` is unique and validated by `^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$` when model validation runs. Plain ORM save does not call full validation.
- Edge cases: API hides ident/content; changing ident or deleting row leaves old/current files; first generated hash is dead assignment; text URL behavior differs between model property and API serializer.

### File validation

- Role: reject disallowed filename extension, filename-derived MIME, and oversized upload.
- Input/state: validator receives Django uploaded value and uses `value.name` plus `len(value)`.
- Behavior: extension is lowercased. MIME uses `mimetypes.guess_type(value.name)`, so it is another filename check, not content inspection.
- Output: raises Django `ValidationError` with allowed extensions/types or formatted size.
- Invariants: configured maximum allows exactly the limit; minimum defaults to zero, so zero-byte audio/video files can pass this validator.
- Edge cases: renamed arbitrary bytes can pass audio/video checks. Image admin forms gain Pillow verification from `ImageField`; audio/video have no magic-byte or decoder validation. Direct ORM saves bypass validators.

### Storage adapter

- Role: local filesystem storage with stable caller-supplied name.
- Startup effect: importing `assets.storages` synchronously creates `/media/audio`, `/media/video`, `/media/image`, and `/media/text`.
- Behavior: `get_available_name()` deletes an existing path with `os.remove()` and then delegates to `FileSystemStorage`.
- Invariants: application processes must have write permission on absolute `/media`; migration imports instantiate the same storage classes and paths.
- Edge cases: delete and replacement are not atomic; failures are not recovered; direct `os.remove()` bypasses storage abstraction; concurrent same-name saves race. Worker/scheduler containers do not mount the shared `files_volume` but still import installed asset models and may create private `/media` directories.

### API

- Routes: full list/create/retrieve/update/partial-update/destroy for `textfile`, `imagefile`, `audiofile`, `videofile`, `hackgame`, and `userinput` beneath `/api/assets/`.
- Lookup IDs: file and user-input detail routes use UUID; hack-game detail uses integer ID.
- Payload omission: every serializer excludes its primary key, so list responses do not expose identifiers needed to construct detail/update/delete URLs.
- Binary payload: `name` plus read-only absolute `file`; UUID and hash excluded.
- Text payload: `name` and nullable file URL; UUID, hash, ident, and content excluded.
- Hack payload: attempts, difficulty, wordcount, chance; ID excluded. Difficulty choices are 6, 8, 10, or 12; other integer fields have no domain bounds.
- User-input payload: action, expected, delay; UUID excluded. Action is unique and defaults to `action`; expected defaults empty; delay defaults 0 and permits null/negative integers.
- Ordering/pagination: querysets have no explicit ordering; app defines no pagination.
- Access policy: every view declares `ModelViewSet` before `DynamicAuthMixin`, so DRF superclass hooks win and the mixin is ineffective. Project defines authentication classes but no authenticated permission; default `AllowAny` makes full asset CRUD public at application level. Auth middleware enforcement is commented out.

### URI and downstream wire behavior

- Binary serializer builds URL with `request.build_absolute_uri(obj.file.path)`. It depends on local filesystem `.path`, exposes the repeated physical path, and cannot support non-filesystem storage.
- Model `uri` uses configured `BASE_URL`, while API binary output uses request host. These authorities can disagree.
- Text serializer uses normal DRF `FileField` URL behavior, based on storage `base_url`/relative `MEDIA_URL`; it does not use physical `.path`. With storage rooted at `/media/text/` plus name `text/...`, generated URL can omit one physical `text` segment or resolve relative to the current request path.
- Nested behavior serializers expose binary/text asset payloads in menu and terminal-account responses. Binary method field requires a serializer context containing `request`; background serialization without it raises `KeyError`.
- Asset save changes menu/account hash inputs but publishes no device-update event. Clients can remain stale until another refresh occurs.

### Relational deletion

- Each concrete menu item references its asset with `on_delete=CASCADE`.
- Deleting an asset deletes referencing menu-item child/base rows and can remove those items from terminal-account menus.
- Deleting a menu item does not delete its asset.
- Django model deletion does not remove `FileField` bytes. Database/file lifecycle is asymmetric in both directions.

## 5. Failure Model

| Failure | Current outcome | Required outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/media` cannot be created/written during import | Django startup, migration import, worker, or command can fail | Provision storage outside module import; fail readiness with explicit diagnostics |
| Public caller mutates/deletes asset | Operation allowed by default `AllowAny`; related menu rows may cascade | Require explicit operator permission; separate read delivery from management |
| Binary API create | File cannot be submitted; empty-file row may persist, then response raises | Accept validated multipart upload or make endpoint read-only |
| Text API create | Hidden ident/content become empty; first bad row/file may persist, later unique failure | Expose valid text command or make endpoint read-only |
| Same binary basename uploaded twice | Existing blob deleted/replaced; multiple rows point at changed shared bytes | UUID/content-addressed storage names; reject or version explicitly |
| Blob write succeeds, DB save fails | Orphan blob remains | Staged write plus commit/finalize/cleanup policy |
| Existing blob deleted, replacement write fails | Previous content lost while DB still references path | Atomic replacement/versioned immutable blobs |
| Asset row deleted | Blob remains; referencing menu rows cascade-delete | Explicit protected/cascade policy plus transactional/reference-aware blob cleanup |
| File content spoofed by extension | Audio/video validator accepts renamed bytes | Content sniff/decoder validation and safe serving headers |
| Missing/corrupt file serialized | `.path`/URL access raises; API/menu response fails | Typed unavailable state and repair/report path |
| Hash expected to represent content | Time-based hash changes without content change or misses same-second change | Content digest or explicit monotonically versioned contract |
| Production requests media | Nginx proxies to Django, which has no production static media route | Dedicated media alias/object store with shared volume and access policy |
| Relative/inconsistent media URL | Different serializers/properties produce different or broken URLs | One storage-generated canonical URL policy |
| Concurrent same-name upload | Delete/write races; final bytes nondeterministic | Immutable unique key plus serialized metadata update |
| Duplicate default `UserInput` or invalid game values | DB uniqueness/incoherent configuration error | Domain validation and clear conflict response |

- Concurrency/order: no storage lock, object version, checksum precondition, transaction/outbox, or cleanup queue exists. Database commit and filesystem operations cannot be atomic. List order is unspecified.
- Reliability: no blob existence health check, orphan reconciliation, backup/versioning, upload status, retry, or compensating cleanup exists. Overwrite destroys recovery point before new write succeeds.
- Security/operations: public CRUD plus cascade delete is high-impact. File checks trust names, media delivery headers are unspecified, and CORS allows all origins. Absolute local storage paths and module-import directory creation tie every process to one deployment layout.

## 6. Gaps

- Tests: no tests cover models, validators, storage, API, admin, media serving, hashes, deletion, menu serialization, or concurrency.
- Docs: no asset-management or media-serving documentation exists; operating-doc images are repository documentation assets, not this app's runtime assets.
- Validation: allowed codecs/content, zero-byte policy, game bounds, user-input delay bounds, filename normalization, duplicate basename policy, and text encoding are not explicitly defined.
- API/schema: generated OpenAPI advertises full writable CRUD while binary file is read-only and all primary keys are omitted. Text schema hides its source fields. No lifecycle or cascade semantics appear.
- Deployment: only API container mounts `files_volume`; Nginx proxies media instead of mounting it; production Django does not serve media. Worker containers import hard-coded storage without shared media.
- Defects: import-time filesystem mutation, repeated path segments, destructive basename overwrite, broken binary/text create endpoints, inconsistent URLs, time-based non-content hash, orphan blobs, cascade surprises, ineffective auth mixin, and missing response IDs.
- Dead/uncertain behavior: no source-code consumer of `HackGame` was found. `TerminalAccount.has_files` references `item.option`, but no such model property was found and the property has no source caller.

## 7. Candidate Target Mapping

Non-authoritative candidate mapping. `20-migration-roadmap.md` owns phase order; generic writable REST is transitional.

| Target component | Responsibility | Constraints |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `AssetMetadataRepository` | Persist UUID, display name, type, content digest/version, and storage key | No filesystem calls in model save; preserve UUID/FK compatibility |
| `BlobStorage` | Stage, finalize, open, URL, and delete immutable blobs | Configured root/backend; no import-time writes; atomic/versioned naming |
| `AssetUploadService` | Authorize, validate content, write blob, persist metadata, compensate failures | Bounded streaming; explicit idempotency and duplicate policy |
| `TextAssetRenderer` | Validate ident/content and generate UTF-8 blob | Deterministic versioned output; old-version cleanup policy |
| `AssetDeliveryService` | Return canonical public/private URLs and availability state | Same semantics for direct and nested serialization; backend-independent |
| `AssetReferencePolicy` | Decide protected deletion versus cascade and report consumers | Preserve menu integrity; cleanup only after commit |
| `GameConfigService` | Validate and serve hack-game settings | Explicit singleton/multi-row ownership and numeric bounds |
| `UserInputService` | Validate action/expected/delay commands | Preserve unique action and UUID identity; explicit delay units/range |

## 8. Roadmap Mapping

`20-migration-roadmap.md` owns order. Map characterization to P0, API/admin decisions to P2, storage migration to P6, and cleanup to P7.

1. Characterize valid admin uploads, existing storage keys/URLs, nested menu payloads, hashes, and every create/update/delete failure.
2. Lock asset mutations behind explicit permissions and disable broken API write paths until characterized.
3. Make blob write, metadata commit, media availability, and cleanup outcomes observable.
4. Introduce configured immutable storage keys and canonical URL generation while retaining legacy-read fallback.
5. Extract upload/text rendering, content validation, repositories, and reference-aware deletion from model `save()`.
6. Backfill content digests/versions and migrate existing repeated-path blobs without breaking menu references.
7. Remove hard-coded `/media`, delete-before-save storage, local `.path` serialization, and legacy routes after compatibility verification.

## 9. Minimum Tests

- Admin upload success for each supported audio/video/image extension and exact size boundaries.
- Extension mismatch, uppercase extension, MIME/content mismatch, corrupt image, zero-byte file, oversized file, and unsafe filename.
- Binary API list/retrieve plus explicit read-only or corrected multipart create/update behavior.
- Text create/update with ident/content, Unicode, ident validation, rename, same-path replacement, and rollback.
- UUID/ID presence in list/detail payloads and route round-trip for every viewset.
- Public/anonymous, authenticated non-operator, and operator read/write/delete permissions.
- Same basename across records, concurrent uploads, failed replacement, DB failure after write, and retry/idempotency.
- Hash changes only under approved content/version rules; menu/account/device hash propagation and refresh.
- Delete with zero/one/many menu references; blob cleanup after commit; orphan reconciliation.
- Development and production media URL/download behavior behind Nginx, including exact content type and security headers.
- Hack-game choices/bounds and user-input uniqueness/default/delay policy.
- Wire/schema compatibility for nested audio/video/image/text/user-input menu payloads.

## 10. Unverified / Decision Required

- Confirm deployed media URL behavior and terminal consumers before preserving any current URL generator.
- Decide referenced-asset deletion, duplicate-basename, and legacy blob-recovery policies before P6 cutover.
- Confirm whether `HackGame` has a live consumer.
- Confirm terminal/client dependency on current asset and menu hash values before defining replacement revision compatibility.

## 11. Confirmed Do-Not-Lose

- Existing UUID primary keys for audio, video, image, text, and user-input records; integer IDs for hack-game rows.
- Existing menu-item foreign-key relationships until an explicit deletion policy is accepted.
- Display name, text ident/content, user-input action/expected/delay, and hack-game setting compatibility.
- Supported extension and size contracts until clients/operators receive a versioned replacement.
- Leading storage/media compatibility for existing database file names and physical blobs during migration.
- Menu payload fields consumed by terminal clients: timer, label, nested content name/file, input label, and input description.
- Required ability to preview/manage assets in custom admin and deliver them to game clients.
